# The quantum speed limit and the discrete light cone. There is a floor on how fast a state can change into a
# distinguishable one, the Mandelstam-Tamm and Margolus-Levitin bounds, set by the energy spread and the mean energy. On
# the substrate this becomes a strict combinatorial wall: the discrete-time walk moves at most one cell per beat, so after
# t beats the influence of a site cannot reach beyond radius t, and the set of reachable cells in one dimension is the
# interval of radius t, two t plus one cells wide. This is the lattice light cone, a Lieb-Robinson bound with a hard front
# that advances one cell per beat. This file DEFINES the width of the light cone after a given number of beats and PROVES
# that it grows by exactly two cells with each beat, one on each side, so the front moves at a fixed maximum speed. It
# records, as machine-integer facts, the cone width at five beats and that a site beyond the front is causally excluded.
# The growth law is proved for every beat count by the ring normalizer.

# The width of the one-dimensional light cone after n beats, defined by the recurrence that each beat adds two cells, one
# on each side, starting from the single origin cell at zero beats.
task cone-width
  take n, like natural-number
  like natural-number
  send back
    fork test
      hook test
        call is-equal
          read n
          code 0
      hook hold
        code 1
      hook miss
        call add
          code 2
          call cone-width
            call subtract
              read n
              code 1

# THE LIGHT CONE IS TWO N PLUS ONE CELLS WIDE: the closed form of the recurrence is cone-width(n) = 2 * n + 1, for every
# beat count n, the interval of radius n. So the front, growing two cells per beat, one on each side, advances at a fixed
# one cell per beat, the ballistic speed limit. Proved for all n by the commutative-ring normalizer.
rule the-cone-is-two-n-plus-one-cells-wide
  seat n, like natural-number
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call cone-width
        read n
      call add
        call multiply
          code 2
          read n
        code 1
  fold n

# THE CONE WIDTH AT FIVE BEATS is eleven cells, the interval of radius five: 2 * 5 + 1 = 11.
hold cone-width-at-five-beats-is-eleven
  call is-equal
    code 11
    call add
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 5
      code 1

# A SITE BEYOND THE FRONT IS CAUSALLY EXCLUDED: a site at distance six is outside the radius-five cone, 6 above 5, so no
# signal reaches it within five beats, the discrete speed limit enforced.
hold a-site-beyond-the-front-is-excluded
  call is-above
    code 6
    code 5
